; Accounts. Assets are split by owner (Me / Co); income and expenses are not: all money is yours,
; and the paying account already shows who paid.
; `iban` metadata tells the importer which account a statement belongs to, and marks transfers
; between own accounts (they go through Assets:Transit, which must return to 0).
; `statements_until`: the last day with imported history; later transfers to it go through rules.
; `ibkr`: the Interactive Brokers account number; securities go to the sibling account `:Securities`.
; Record what you know about an account (who, why) as a comment next to it: it is the memory.

; 2000-01-01 open Assets:Me:Bank:Current EUR
;   iban: "SK0000000000000000000000"
; 2000-01-01 open Assets:Co:Bank:Current EUR
;   iban: "SK0000000000000000000000"
; 2000-01-01 open Assets:Me:Broker:Cash
;   ibkr: "U0000000"
; 2000-01-01 open Assets:Me:Broker:Securities "FIFO"

2000-01-01 open Assets:Transit  ; transfers between own accounts
2000-01-01 open Equity:Opening-Balances
2000-01-01 open Equity:Conversions  ; exchanges between own accounts in different currencies

2000-01-01 open Income:Clients
2000-01-01 open Income:Benefits
2000-01-01 open Income:Family
2000-01-01 open Income:Inheritance
2000-01-01 open Income:Investments:Gains
2000-01-01 open Income:Investments:Interest
2000-01-01 open Income:Other
2000-01-01 open Income:Uncategorized

; `need` on expense accounts groups spending for the baseline queries in Fava:
; essential (fixed by contract or law), flexible (needed, can be reduced), optional (luxury, can stop),
; income-linked (stops with the income), unknown (mixed: cash, card, uncategorized).
; `cut` on flexible and unknown accounts: the share still paid after cutting back.
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Food:Groceries
  need: "flexible"
  cut: 0.7
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Food:Restaurants
  need: "optional"
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Housing:Interest
  need: "essential"
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Housing:Garden
  need: "optional"
